  "worked_solution": "A quadrilateral has $n=4$ sides. Therefore, the sum of the interior angles of a quadrilateral must be \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{180}^{∘}\\cdot (n-2) & ={180}^{∘}\\cdot (4-2) \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & ={360}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding up the internal angles and solving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠A+m∠B+m∠C+m∠D & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ (x+{90}^{∘})+(4x-{17}^{∘})+(3x+{3}^{∘})+{60}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 8x+{136}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 8x & ={224}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={28}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
